# 17. K-Means vs DBSCAN

| Feature | K-Means | DBSCAN |
|---|---|---|
| Need K beforehand? | Yes | No |
| Handles arbitrary shapes? | Limited | Better |
| Handles noise? | Limited | Yes |
| Outlier handling | Sensitive | Can identify noise |
| Cluster density | Assumes relatively compatible structure | Works well for density-based clusters |

---

# 18. K-Means vs Hierarchical Clustering

| K-Means | Hierarchical |
|---|---|
| Flat clusters | Hierarchy of clusters |
| Requires K beforehand | Can inspect dendrogram |
| Generally efficient | Can become expensive for large datasets |
| Centroid-based | Distance/linkage-based hierarchy |

