# 23. Top 3 Interview Questions 🎯

## Q1. Why is K-Means called K-Means?

> **K** represents the number of clusters, and **Means** refers to calculating the mean of data points in each cluster to update the centroid.

---

## Q2. Why is feature scaling important for K-Means?

> K-Means relies on distance calculations. Features with larger numerical ranges can dominate the distance calculation, causing the clustering process to be biased toward those features.

---

## Q3. How do you choose K?

> I would use techniques such as the Elbow Method and Silhouette Score, while also considering domain knowledge, cluster stability, and business usefulness.

